tadottama-vidāṁ lokān
amalān pratipadyate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3908,\"bb\":3438,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/14/b3438/\",\"shadow_value\":\"yadā – when; sattve – the mode of goodness; pravṛddhe – developed; tu – but; pralayam – dissolution; yāti – goes; deha-bhṛt – the embodied; tadā – at that time; uttama-vidām – of the great sages; lokān – the planets; amalān – pure; pratipadyate – attains.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"yadā\",\"translation\":\"when\"},{\"word\":\"sattve\",\"translation\":\"the mode of goodness\"},{\"word\":\"pravṛddhe\",\"translation\":\"developed\"},{\"word\":\"tu\",\"translation\":\"but\"},{\"word\":\"pralayam\",\"translation\":\"dissolution\"},{\"word\":\"yāti\",\"translation\":\"goes\"},{\"word\":\"deha-bhṛt\",\"translation\":\"the embodied\"},{\"word\":\"tadā\",\"translation\":\"at that time\"},{\"word\":\"uttama-vidām\",\"translation\":\"of the great sages\"},{\"word\":\"lokān\",\"translation\":\"the planets\"},{\"word\":\"amalān\",\"translation\":\"pure\"},{\"word\":\"pratipadyate\",\"translation\":\"attains\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3909,\"bb\":3439,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/14/b3439/\",\"body_value\":\"When one dies in the mode of goodness, he attains to the pure higher planets of the great sages.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3910,\"bb\":3440,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/14/b3440/\",\"body_value\":\"One in goodness attains higher planetary systems, like Brahmaloka or Janaloka, and there enjoys godly happiness. The word amalān is significant; it means “free from the modes of passion and ignorance.” There are impurities in the material world, but the mode of goodness is